---
// Instructions vs. data: trusted channels (system, user) carry authority over the agent; untrusted external content is wrapped in a source tag before entering the context; Skills and status-bar sources are new surfaces loaded as instructions or trusted, with their own defenses; the context layer is only the first line of defense.
---

<svg
	class="dg"
	viewBox="0 0 720 616"
	role="img"
	aria-labelledby="d2-idb-title d2-idb-desc"
	style="min-width: 630px"
>
	<title id="d2-idb-title">Separating instructions from data</title>
	<desc id="d2-idb-desc">
		Top left: trusted channels, the system prompt and the user's direct request, sent in their own Chat Template roles.
		Top right: untrusted external content, each item wrapped in an external_content tag that annotates its source: web
		page hidden text, email, PDF metadata and image EXIF metadata. Below them, new surfaces that are loaded as
		instructions or trusted, so source tagging does not neutralize them: a third-party Skill, which must be reviewed
		before install, and a status-bar source, which should come only from controlled sources. All three flow into the
		context: the trusted channels through structured roles, the external content through the tool role and input
		sanitization, which is auxiliary only. In the context, instructions carry authority and data is only material to
		be processed. A banner notes that the context layer is only the first line of defense; the execution and data
		layers are in lesson 1.8 and later chapters.
	</desc>
	<defs>
		<marker id="d2-idb-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto-start-reverse">
			<path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="dg-arrowhead"></path>
		</marker>
	</defs>

	<text x="2" y="28" class="dg-title">Separating instructions from data</text>

	<!-- Top left: trusted channels -->
	<g class="dg-container dg-harness">
		<rect x="2" y="44" width="220" height="190" rx="12"></rect>
		<text x="14" y="72" font-weight="700">Trusted channels</text>
		<text x="14" y="94" class="dg-sub">may direct behavior</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-harness">
		<rect x="14" y="104" width="196" height="56" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="30" y="126" class="dg-accent" font-weight="700">system</text>
		<text x="30" y="148" class="dg-sub">system prompt</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-harness">
		<rect x="14" y="168" width="196" height="56" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="30" y="190" class="dg-accent" font-weight="700">user</text>
		<text x="30" y="212" class="dg-sub">direct user request</text>
	</g>

	<!-- Top right: untrusted content, wrapped in source tags -->
	<g class="dg-container dg-guard">
		<rect x="246" y="44" width="472" height="190" rx="12"></rect>
		<text x="258" y="72" font-weight="700">&lt;external_content source="…"&gt;</text>
		<text x="258" y="94" class="dg-sub">untrusted: material, not instructions</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-env">
		<rect x="258" y="110" width="220" height="48" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="274" y="140">Web page hidden text</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-env">
		<rect x="490" y="110" width="216" height="48" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="506" y="140">Email</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-env">
		<rect x="258" y="170" width="220" height="48" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="274" y="200">PDF metadata</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-env">
		<rect x="490" y="170" width="216" height="48" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="506" y="200">Image EXIF metadata</text>
	</g>

	<!-- Middle: new surfaces that source tagging does not cover -->
	<g class="dg-container dg-env">
		<rect x="162" y="272" width="470" height="148" rx="12"></rect>
		<text x="174" y="300" font-weight="700">New surfaces: loaded as instructions or trusted</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-env">
		<rect x="174" y="314" width="446" height="44" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="190" y="342"><tspan font-weight="700">Third-party Skill:</tspan> review before install</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-env">
		<rect x="174" y="366" width="446" height="44" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="190" y="394"><tspan font-weight="700">Status-bar source:</tspan> trust only controlled sources</text>
	</g>

	<!-- Context -->
	<g class="dg-node dg-context">
		<rect x="2" y="450" width="716" height="72" rx="10"></rect>
		<text x="18" y="478" class="dg-accent" font-weight="700">Context</text>
		<text x="18" y="504" class="dg-sub">instructions carry authority; data is only material to be processed</text>
	</g>

	<g class="dg-edge">
		<line x1="80" y1="234" x2="80" y2="448" marker-end="url(#d2-idb-arrow)"></line>
		<text x="92" y="256" class="dg-edge-label">structured roles</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-edge">
		<line x1="680" y1="234" x2="680" y2="448" marker-end="url(#d2-idb-arrow)"></line>
		<text x="668" y="256" text-anchor="end" class="dg-edge-label">tool role · sanitization (auxiliary)</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-edge">
		<line x1="397" y1="420" x2="397" y2="448" marker-end="url(#d2-idb-arrow)"></line>
	</g>

	<!-- Banner -->
	<g class="dg-node dg-neutral">
		<rect x="2" y="540" width="716" height="72" rx="10"></rect>
		<text x="18" y="568" font-weight="700">Context layer = first line of defense only</text>
		<text x="18" y="594" class="dg-sub">Execution and data layers: lesson 1.8 and later chapters</text>
	</g>
</svg>
